0.21.353.112 D srv  log_server_r: request:  {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Estimate the probability that the complete original answer contains any span unsupported by its original source. The target always refers to the ORIGINAL source, even when source evidence has been erased. Erasure removes information and does not change the answer's correctness. Return only a JSON object with unsupported_probability and source_sentence_id. Use null when no visible source sentence is a proposed witness."}, {"role": "user", "content": "{\"complete_source\": \"\", \"original_answer\": \"Louis Jordan, a 37-year-old man from Conway, South Carolina, was found alive after spending 66 days lost at sea. Jordan had set out on a fishing trip in his 35-foot sailboat, but a storm caused the boat to capsize and his mast to break. With a broken shoulder, Jordan was unable to fix the boat and was left drifting in the ocean. After enduring multiple capsizes and storms, Jordan's food and water eventually ran out, and he struggled to collect fresh water due to the rough conditions. However, he managed to attract fish using his laundry, which he would put out to sea for rinsing. Jordan was eventually spotted by the crew of the Houston Express, a container ship, and was rescued. Despite his ordeal, Jordan was in surprisingly good condition when found and had not lost much weight or suffered severe sunburns. Coast Guard officials confirmed his incredible story and noted that his father had reported him and his boat missing on January 29. Jordan's father praised his son's strength and spirituality, saying that he had prayed throughout his ordeal. Jordan is expected to return to his boat in the near future.\", \"target\": \"any_unsupported_span_in_original_response\", \"visible_source_sentence_ids\": [], \"source_evidence_erased\": true}"}], "add_generation_prompt": true, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
